cp - copy regular files

SYNOPSIS
    cp source target
    cp source ... directory

DESCRIPTION
    Copy the contents of a regular file. With a directory target, use
    the basename of each source to choose its destination. Existing
    destination files are truncated. Source and target must have
    different inodes. When a source fails, cp tries the remaining
    operands.

EXIT STATUS
    Zero on success, one on a copy error, or two for invalid usage.

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), cmp(1), mv(1), umask(1)
